# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository *and* the working tree.
#
# Why: this project's toolchain is WSL2/Linux Go plus Linux CI, so every
# tool that writes a file (gofmt, `go test` updating golden files, etc.)
# produces LF. Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true in its system
# config, which smudges the whole checkout to CRLF on clone — so every file
# the WSL toolchain then rewrites shows up as a phantom whole-file
# "modification" in `git status` with a zero-line content diff. Pinning
# eol=lf here makes autocrlf a no-op for this repo and stops that churn on
# any platform. See docs/04-environment-and-testing.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
